+# Improving the one-turn design question round without a second round (analysis, 2026-11-18)
+
+Lane C30K-K25. Read-only analysis, no code, no test run. Source: the queue open item "design-round improvement inside the existing one-turn question round (no second round)" (`candidate-30-queue-2026-11-15.md` line 571) and the 30k plan row (`candidate-30k-plan-2026-11-18.md` line 29). Neither gives a specification, so this document fixes the reading first.
+
+Labels: **PROVEN** = read in the named file and line in this tree. **INFERRED** = a reading that no test or run confirms. Paths are repository-relative. Line numbers of plugin code, references, roles, tests and `harness/verify-suites.json` were re-read in the scratch clone of the integrated tree (30i and 30j chains plus the 30k wave 1 lanes), the tree this patch is a delta on. Plan, queue and backlog files were read in the repository checkout and not re-read in the clone.
+
+## 0. Which "round" this is
+
+- **Reading used (INFERRED from wording, PROVEN for the mechanism):** the "one-turn question round" is the one bundled round of design questions of fresh-repository intake. Its text says "exactly ONE bundled round; a second round with different answers is refused" (`plugins/pipeline-core/skills/pipeline-start/references/intake-generate-design.md` line 54) and "Ask the design questions in one round" (same file line 93). The writer enforces it: a different answer set after the round is refused `INTAKE-DESIGN-QUESTIONS-ALREADY-ANSWERED` (`plugins/pipeline-core/lib/onboarding-continuity.mjs` line 7318).
+- **Reading excluded:** the independent design REVIEW rounds (one full plus two delta rounds, C30-6, `candidate-30-queue-2026-11-15.md` lines 77 to 148; `design-course.md` lines 97 to 125). Those are already capped by the PO and are not a question round. If the PO meant them, this document does not apply (open decision D1).
+
+## 1. (a) What the round is today, and the defects observed
+
+**The mechanism (PROVEN).**
+
+- Status `intake-design-questions-required`, transaction state `design-questions-pending`, is reached after the first material capture (`plugins/pipeline-core/lib/project-onboarding-v3.mjs` lines 4026 to 4037, call at line 4030).
+- The returned action is one `collect-input` whose whole guidance is: "ask the PO the ONE bundled round of design questions this project still needs answered ... Never invent an answer, reconstruct the command, or ask a second round" (same file lines 3300 to 3317, text on line 3306). It names the answer file route `scratch/design-answers.json`.
+- The guidance carries no question list, no ordering, no default, no shape. The agent authors every question.
+- The writer accepts a JSON array of `{question, answer}` or `{"disposition":"no-open-questions"}`; an empty set is refused; every answer must be non-blank (`onboarding-continuity.mjs` lines 7279 to 7283, entry check lines 6778 to 6783).
+- A wrong set can be replaced only while the state is `ready-to-generate` (`intake-design-questions-replace`, lines 7308 to 7317; `docs/v3-consumer-onboarding.md` lines 125 to 128). That is a correction, not a second question round.
+- Recording: the checkpoint holds question and answer privately; the tracked `design-input.md` lists the question text only; the answers appear only in the git-ignored authoring copy (`onboarding-continuity.mjs` lines 7471 to 7480 and 7906 to 7908; `intake-generate-design.md` lines 124 to 129 and 154 to 165).
+- Turn budget (PROVEN, `intake-generate-design.md` lines 80 to 98): the first round is one PO turn; Claude takes at most 3 PO turns before the first design draft, Codex and Antigravity at most 2. The design questions are one of those turns.
+- When the PO adopts the agent's recommendations, each question is recorded with the adopted answer (`intake-generate-design.md` lines 93 to 96, added by commit `15bc32ddf`).
+
+**Defects observed (each cited; none invented).**
+
