+| F3 | A wrong test answer became immutable | `backlog/items/2026-09-10-onboarding-design-answers-have-no-pre-generation-correction-path.md` | Closed (replace route) |
+| F4 | An agent asked five or six bootstrap questions one at a time | `backlog/items/2026-08-29-bootstrap-po-questions-asked-sequentially-instead-of-in-one-block.md`; fix was text only, a self-check for the BOOTSTRAP questions (`kickoff-design.md` lines 135 to 142) | Closed for the bootstrap step. **Not carried to the design questions** (PROVEN: the self-check names "language, goal, profile", lines 137 to 139) |
+| F5 | A question that carries an address or e-mail lands unchecked in `design-input.md` | `candidate-19-plan-2026-11-02.md` line 131 (row E5) | The e-mail case is handled in code: question text passes through a path and e-mail projection before it reaches `design-input.md` (`onboarding-continuity.mjs` lines 7457 to 7468 and 7480). INFERRED that this is what row E5 asked for; whether the same check covers other private identifiers is not read |
+
+Two further complaints sit next to the round and are NOT about it, so they are left out: the twelve-module drift came from repeated decomposition questions in the design REVIEW (`candidate-30-queue-2026-11-15.md` lines 173 to 174, C30-6), and the four-round count of the guided init (`backlog/items/2026-08-28-the-guided-init-asks-the-po-four-times-where-three-is-the-floor.md`) is closed by the merged first round.
+
+**Existing rules that already describe a good question and are not applied to this round (PROVEN):**
+
+- Decision questions are numbered and inline, each with a default recommendation; a question-UI tool only for a binary 1 to 2 line gate (`roles/elephant.md` EL-17 (a) and (b), lines 327 to 335).
+- Problem, options, consequence of each, recommendation, in plain language (EL-29, lines 337 to 358).
+- A worked example of the plain-language shape for a profile or language question (`kickoff-design.md` lines 72 to 84 and 123 to 129).
+- Material design choices go to the PO as "concise Chat tiles with options, tradeoffs and a recommendation" (`design-course.md` lines 9 to 11; `skills/architecture-decision/SKILL.md` lines 32 to 34; `templates/prompts/elephant-kickoff.md` lines 151 to 156). INFERRED conflict: EL-17 (b) restricts question-UI tools to binary gates while the design course names "tiles"; the files do not say whether a tile is a UI tool or a chat message.
+
+The round's guidance cites none of these (PROVEN, line 3306), so the shape of the one round is left to the model each time.
