+## 2. (b) Improvements that stay inside ONE turn
+
+Each is text or a derived read. None adds a stored status, a record field, a digest, a gate or a second question message. "Reader" means an existing function that reads existing state.
+
+| # | Improvement | Change | Cost |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| I1 | **A minimal question set, derived from the stored profile.** The guidance names the topics the agent must cover for `feature` and `epic` (users, core flow, constraints, out of scope, success signal) and says `mini` needs none unless the material leaves a gap. The agent may add questions | A reader: `intakeDesignQuestionsAction` gets the profile from the checkpoint it is already handed (`checkpoint.value.values.profile`, stored at `onboarding-continuity.mjs` lines 6820 and 7129, checkpoint read at `project-onboarding-v3.mjs` line 3951 and in scope at the call, line 4030). Derived at read time, stored nowhere. This is the F1 default, which the PO's list already proceeded with unless vetoed | One function parameter plus a string table. No record, no argv, no digest |
+| I2 | **A recommended default shown with every question.** One line per question: the recommended answer and why | Text of the guidance and of `intake-generate-design.md`. It strengthens an existing sentence ("when the PO adopts your recommendations", `intake-generate-design.md` lines 93 to 96), which presupposes recommendations but never requires them | Text only. Reuses EL-17 (a) and EL-29 |
+| I3 | **A short consequence line per option**, not a table | Text | Text only |
+| I4 | **Order: material gaps first, nice-to-know last, so "adopt all defaults" is one reply.** The PO can answer in one line | Text | Text only |
+| I5 | **Batching self-check for the design questions** (the F4 fix carried over): list every question, confirm the list is complete, send them in ONE message, never one at a time | Text, one paragraph in `intake-generate-design.md` next to line 93 | Text only |
+| I6 | **Do not ask what the captured material already answers**; record that point as a question whose answer cites it ("stated in the material: ...") only when the writer needs a non-blank answer | Text | Text only; the writer already requires non-blank answers (line 6780) |
+| I7 | **Record the answers once, straight from the single reply** into `scratch/design-answers.json`, with an adopted default stored as that default's text (already the rule, `intake-generate-design.md` lines 93 to 96) | Text: say it in the guidance, not only in the reference | Text only |
+| I8 | **Resolve the tile versus message ambiguity** for this round: one numbered chat message with defaults, no question-UI tool (EL-17 (b)) | One sentence | Text only; needs a PO word (D3) |
+
+What each changes: I1 changes a returned guidance string and its input (a reader). I2 to I8 change prose the agent reads. No record, no checkpoint shape, no key bytes, no gate, no signature, no approval, no Critic evidence, no security scan, no audit-bundle semantics change. Nothing is deleted.
