+## 3. (c) What would need a second round, so is NOT proposed
+
+- A follow-up clarification after the PO's answers, or a "round 2 of design questions". Refused by design (`onboarding-continuity.mjs` line 7318) and by the PO's wish.
+- Asking per-question tiles one at a time. It is a sequence of turns (F4).
+- Moving questions to after generation, or asking the PO to answer questions about the drafted PRD. The PO acknowledgement of the draft is already round 4 of the guided init and must not be automated away (`backlog/items/2026-08-28-the-guided-init-asks-the-po-four-times-where-three-is-the-floor.md` lines 46 to 51).
+- Splitting questions into "ask now" and "ask later" with a status per question. It needs a stored status (banned: DO-NOT-DO 12 of `state-machine-simplification-analysis-2026-11-17.md` line 303).
+- Merging the design-question answers with the later architecture tile selections (`--selection` file, `skills/architecture-decision/SKILL.md` lines 94 to 97). Two records exist for two purposes; merging changes a record shape and a bound digest (DO-NOT-DO 3).
+- An agent-run automatic `replace` after it reads its own draft. The replace route stays a PO-visible correction before generation.
+
